#HELPS

0 CLASSES KITS CLASSKITS~
GENESIS: 2k26 | CLASS GUIDE | 19 standalone parent classes

Class         Progression / identity                  Help topic
------------  --------------------------------------  ------------
Angel         Angel mastery and support               ANGEL
Cyborg        Components, systems and nanites          CYBORG
Deathknight   Deathbound mastery and soul energy      DEATHKNIGHT
Demon         Unified mastery, souls and pacts         DEMON
Dragon        Dragon skills and transformation        DRAGON
Drow          Prayer, disciplines and favor           DROW
Elemental     Independent elemental tracks            ELEMENTAL
Gargoyle      Visceratika and stone energy            GARGOYLE
Highlander    Blademastery and weapon progression     HIGHLANDER
Kuei-jin      Chi, Dharma and discipline tracks       KUEIJIN
Mage          Arete, spheres and quintessence          MAGE
Monk          Martial and spiritual training          MONK
Moogle        Pom mastery and supportive magic        MOOGLE
Ninja         Principles, michi and Ki                NINJA
Phoenix       Phoenix mastery                         PHOENIX
Sorcerer      Written spells and book colors          BOOKMAGIC
Vampire       Generation, blood and disciplines       VAMPIRE
Werewolf      Breed, auspice and tribe gifts          WEREWOLF
Wraith        Arcanoi and pathos                      WRAITH

Use AUTOCLASS to inspect entry requirements and AUTOCLASS <class> to join.
Sorcerer is the book mage; Mage is the separate sphere/Arete class.
Chaos Book Mage is a Sorcerer playstyle, not a twentieth hybrid parent.
Use HELP <topic> for details. HELP CLASSMENUS explains the table displays.
Hybrid conversion, ascension and respec are not currently enabled.
~

0 VAMPIRE VAMPIRES VAMPIREKIT~
Vampire uses generation, blood, Beast and disciplines. Use DISCIPLINES
to inspect your character's available training and mastery.
The kit includes Animalism, Auspex, Celerity, Chimerstry, Daimoinon,
Dominate, Fortitude, Melpominee, Mortis, Necromancy, Obfuscate,
Obtenebration, Potence, Presence, Protean, Quietus, Serpentis,
Thaumaturgy and Vicissitude.
Powers retain their blood, form, visibility, target and PK requirements;
learning a discipline does not remove a power's individual prerequisites.
Related: HELP DISCIPLINES, HELP FRENZY, HELP KITSTATUS.
~

0 WEREWOLF WEREWOLVES WEREWOLFKIT~
Werewolf uses breed, auspice and tribe gifts in addition to shapeshifting.
Progression and gift prerequisites remain separate: a tribe gift is not
automatically available merely because another track has been mastered.
The kit includes Primal Anger, Burrow, Spirit Ward, Jam Technology, Blur,
Mother's Touch, Wyld gifts, spirit interaction and tribal attacks/defenses.
Restored gifts use named effects, native costs/saving throws, cooldowns
and the usual protected-target rules.
Related: HELP BREED, HELP AUSPICE, HELP TRIBE, HELP RESTOREDGIFTS.
~

0 SORCERER SORCERERS BOOKMAGE BOOKMAGIC CHAOSMAGE CHAOSBOOKMAGE~
Sorcerer is the book mage, distinct from the sphere-based Mage.
AUTOCLASS SORCERER chooses normal book magic.
AUTOCLASS CHAOSMAGE or AUTOCLASS SORCERER CHAOS chooses Chaos book magic.
Existing Sorcerers may claim their once-per-character kit:
  sorccreate starter
It contains a primer, pen, instruction pages and three finished spells:
  Spark (page 2, targeted damage), Mend (page 3, targeted healing),
  Minor Ward (page 4, protective armor blessing).
  hold primer
  read primer
  turn primer 0
  turn primer 4
  chant self
The index is page 0. Read pages 1 and 5 for navigation and writing/binding.
Normal mages start with at least rank 1 blue/green/yellow; Chaos starts
with all six colors at rank 1. Higher existing mastery is preserved.
Chaos books roll a fresh color on EACH chant; colors may repeat.
Healing remains healing, attacks remain attacks and blessings keep their
written purpose. Travel/action pages keep their written operation.
Spark costs 200 mana, Mend 400, Minor Ward 1560 at normal starter mastery.
Chaos damage/healing costs vary by rolled color. Minor Ward has two ticks
of native duration and RAISES armor: higher armor improves Genesis defense.
Do not put REVERSED on a protective armor script. Same-color wards do not
stack. Read the actual primer for an executable spell-writing recipe.
Other crafting still costs resources. Starter claims cannot be repeated.
Utility: cast ventriloquate pen <message> creates explicit illusory speech.
Related: HELP SORCCREATE, HELP CHANT, HELP WRITE, HELP COLORS.
~

0 MAGE MAGES MAGEKIT~
Mage is the sphere/arete class, NOT the Sorcerer/book mage.
Its kit uses Arete, sphere mastery, quintessence and paradox.
MAGEPOWERS lists your learned abilities; SPHERE <name> shows the real power
menu rather than the old placeholder. SPHERE <name> LEARN trains as before.
Commands include rift, analyze, brittle bones, mutate ephemera, sculpture,
alterweight, invisibility, spirit sense/caress, step sideways, dreamshell,
heart's blood, holy smote, enchantment, paradox ward, healing, better body,
polymorph, friction curse, electrical chaos, inferno and contingency.
Use HELP <ability> for its existing command name and prerequisites.
Friction Curse uses: frictioncurse <target> <nonnegative quintessence>.
It checks costs and target protection before charging and restores the
caster's original room after remote safety validation.
Numeric quintessence inputs are validated before any paradox/cost effects.
Other legacy argument/effect variants remain under verification; HELP KITSTATUS
does not claim that all old sphere spells have been independently certified.
~

0 DROW DROWKIT~
Drow has prayer/disciplines, acid bolt, faeriefire, spider summoning,
globe of darkness, Door, armor and ranged shooting.
Progression, required favor and target/room protections still apply.
Use HELP DROWPOWERS and existing ability help for command details.
Related: HELP PRAY, HELP FAERIEFIRE, HELP KITSTATUS.
~

0 HIGHLANDER HIGHLANDERS HIGHLANDERKIT~
Highlander is the immortal blademaster class. Its kit includes Blade Flash,
Bash, Hilt Twist, Judgement, Lunge and weapon forge/increase progression.
Use HELP FORGE and HELP INCREASE for the existing progression rules.
Weapon, stance and trained-stat requirements remain distinct.
Related: HELP STANCE, HELP SKILL, HELP KITSTATUS.
~

0 DRAGON DRAGONS DRAGONKIT~
Dragon uses dragonform, breath attacks, Dust, tail attacks, horns, wings
and dragon-skill progression. Form and learned-power checks remain required.
Use HELP DRAGONFORM and existing breath/dragon ability help for syntax.
Related: HELP KITSTATUS.
~

0 NINJA NINJAS NINJAKIT~
Ninja uses principles, michi, Ki and stealth/combat progression.
The kit includes Kakusu, Mienaku, Tsumazuku, Tsume, Shuurai,
Hakunetsu, Harakiri and the Bomuzite sleep bomb.
Bomuzite requires its Sora tier and 20 Ki. It cannot sleep self, party
members, protected/non-PK targets or already sleeping targets, and it ends
the relevant native combat state before putting a valid target to sleep.
Related: HELP MICHI, HELP PRINCIPLES, HELP KITSTATUS.
~

0 MONK MONKS MONKKIT~
Monk is the unarmed martial/spiritual class. Its kit includes Aura Shot,
Blitz, Cripple, Darkblaze, Stun Fist, Chimera, Healing Touch, Almighty,
Celestial, Life Cloak and monk training.
Support and group effects require valid recipients and sufficient resources;
an already-active blessing does not justify charging for an empty recast.
Related: HELP MONKTRAIN, HELP KITSTATUS.
~

0 ELEMENTAL ELEMENTALIST ELEMENTALKIT~
Elemental uses independent elemental progression and native timed effects.
Its kit includes Flare Arrow, Fireblade, Icicle Storm, Water Travel,
Aqua Barrier, Wind Wings, Wind Blades, Stone Blast, Local Quake,
Holy Aura, Solar Flash, Ultima Wave, Slow and elemental defenses/senses.
Native effects persist through save/relogin and expire through character
updates. Travel, combat safety and individual prerequisites still apply.
Werewolf command: ELEMENTAL <fire|water|earth|air> <target> instead invokes
the separate Lupus 5 gift; it does not select the Elemental parent.
See HELP WOLFELEMENTAL for that legacy command.
Related: HELP KITSTATUS.
~

0 ANGEL ANGELS ANGELKIT~
Use ANGEL for the live ability menu; ANGEL TRAIN advances mastery to 8.
The kit includes aura, claws, angelform, feet, nightsight, wings, might,
toughness, speed, travel, shadowsight, emergency_inferno, windwall,
heightened_senses, read_aura, spiritshare, strengthen, guardianangel,
purifyspirit, empower, angelarmour and halo.
Reference controls include scry, eyespy, cherub, unveil, astral_projection,
weaponform, humanform, object_move, object_leap, object_magic,
object_lifespan and inpart.
Support requires willing/grouped recipients. Read Aura reports visible
NPC alignment, not a restored player-alignment system.
Object/familiar forms have ownership, room and safe return/cleanup rules.
Use the live menu for rank/cost requirements. Hybrids remain disabled.
~

0 CYBORG CYBORGS CYBORGKIT~
CYBORG | MENU AND COMMAND GUIDE

Display command   Contents
----------------  -----------------------------------------------------
cyborg            Compact resources, training ranks/costs and navigation
cyborg status     Same overview; sys_status and systems are aliases
cyborg implants   All 24 components, costs and installation eligibility
cyborg powers     Component powers, system powers and passive thresholds
cyborg all        All sections together

Every command below requires the CYBORG prefix.

Category      Command / syntax
------------  ---------------------------------------------------------
Installation  install/uninstall <component>; implant/replace <component>
Training      train; bionics <XP>; face_implants improve/show
Training      limb_implants improve/show; body_implants improve/show
Training      demolitions improve/show
Nanites       convert <mana>; factory on/off; repair
Weapons       taser <target>; snipe <target>; launch <target>
Explosives    make_bomb; arm; arm off; detonate <target>; mine
Control       stuntubes <target>; oilspit <target>; web <target>
Forms        cubeform; terminator; cloak; shadowwalk; upload
Senses        mechsight; scry <target>; read_aura <NPC>
Utility       radio <message>; transmit <grouped player>; lloth; darkness
Equipment     cyborgeq <piece>

The kit has 60 inventory entries, NOT 60 different attacks.
24 installed components have dependency, primal and humanity requirements.
Example first install: CYBORG INSTALL BATTERY (30 primal, 5 humanity).
Installation and training require peace, standing and a mortal character.
Staff characters are deliberately blocked; use a mortal test character.
Eligible means component/resource checks pass; it does not bypass those rules.
The normal 100-humanity budget requires a loadout, not installation of every
component simultaneously. Safe uninstall refunds humanity once, never primal.
Rifle and demolitions cap at 12; face/limbs/body at 5/5/6.
Stored nanites cap at 10000, bombs at 20, bionics at 10000000.
Mine is room-bound and defensive; missiles require both legs and targeting.
Snipe is SAME ROOM. Transmit is protected travel to a willing party member.
Oilspit/Stuntubes use removable named poison, not permanent raw flags.
Armor, limb combat modifiers, weapon ceiling, regeneration and vision use
native passive hooks. Total-darkness sight requires face 3 and Mechsight.
Cyborgeq pieces: whip/ring/collar/armor/helmet/leggings/boots/gloves/sleeves/
cloak/belt/bracer/mask; each costs 100 primal and duplicate carried pieces
are refused. Systems persist across save/relogin; deployed mines do not.
The class is a standalone and planned hybrid parent. Conversion remains off.
~

0 CLASSMENUS CLASSMENU POWERMENU~
CLASS MENUS | READING THE TABLES

Column        Meaning
------------  ---------------------------------------------------------
Rank          Required mastery or named track rank
Mana/Energy   Listed resource cost; other action prerequisites still apply
Known         Rank requirement met, not a guarantee the action can run now
Locked        Rank requirement not met
Next cost     Exact price of one next training step, not all remaining ranks
Currency      XP, primal or bionics; Dragon DP/QP and Drow favor are separate
Affordable    Currency check passes; action/state prerequisites still apply
Needs funds   Current balance is below the displayed training price
MAXED         At training cap; -- is not a free upgrade
Need Dharma   Raise Dharma before buying this Kuei-jin track rank
Need body 4   Face level five requires body level four
Need limbs 1  Body training requires at least one limb level
Focus active  Elemental focus prevents further basic training
Passive       Automatic system threshold, not a separate attack to cast
Installed     Component already present
Eligible      Component permissions, dependencies and resources met
Needs parts   Install prerequisite components first
No primal     More primal is required
No humanity   Free humanity is insufficient for this installation

All 19 parent classes have organized tables. Older class commands:
Class         View training          View powers
------------  ---------------------  -------------------------
Vampire       discipline             powers
Werewolf      gifts / tribegifts     powers
Mage          sphere                 magepowers
Dragon        dragonskill            dragonskill
Drow          prayer                 drowupkeep
Elemental     elemskill              elemskill <element>
Highlander    increase               increase
Monk          monklearn              monklearn <track>
Ninja         principle              principle <name>
Sorcerer      colors                 help bookmagic

Newer classes use their class-name command. Cyborg is split into overview,
implants and powers to avoid one long dump. Add improve after a Cyborg system
name to train it; cyborg train improves rifle mastery.

Vampire clan/Caitiff discounts, Werewolf selected-gift discounts and Mage
favored sphere caps are included in the quotes. DP means Dragon class points;
QP means quest points. Dragon age training may require both at once.
Drow favor is the Drow class-point balance, not primal.
Demon gifts quote primal; warps quote soul power, converted from XP 1:1.
SPHERE shows Arete's next XP price safely; ARETE purchases that upgrade.
Gift selection is free and permanent; later gift ranks still cost primal.

Menus are read-only. Looking at a table never trains, spends resources,
installs equipment, changes class or enables a hybrid.
Aliases and existing HELP topics are preserved. HELP KITSTATUS describes
the verification limits; documentation is not full gameplay certification.
~

0 DEMON DEMONS DEMONKIT~
Use DEMON for the live ability menu; DEMON TRAIN advances mastery to 8.
The kit includes fangs, claws, demonform, hooves, wings, horns, tail,
senses, might/toughness/speed, infernal attacks, curses and defensive aspects.
Reference systems include souls, pact, offersoul, champions, inpart, warps,
redeem and gifts. Their consent, authority, resources and variant requirements
are enforced separately; use the live menus instead of guessing grant syntax.
The unified Demon also has familiar/object forms, demon/animal shapes,
weapon enchantments, wards, travel and courier functionality.
Soul/pact powers do not bypass protected players or grant staff authority.
All reference mechanics are Genesis adaptations; hybrid conversion remains off.
~

0 PHOENIX PHOENIXKIT~
Use PHOENIX for the live menu and PHOENIX TRAIN for progression.
Abilities: emberbolt, featherward, flamingwings, ashwalk, phoenixtears,
solarflare, renewal and ascendantaspect.
The kit uses native damage, named timed defenses/flight, healing and bounded
travel. Existing effects cannot stack from duplicate casts or repeated load.
Related: HELP KITSTATUS.
~

0 GARGOYLE GARGOYLEKIT~
Use GARGOYLE for the live menu; visceratika trains the track to 5.
Abilities: stonefist, wings, stone_rest, statue and statue back.
Stone resilience reduces physical damage by 5% per rank, capped at 25%.
Ground awareness starts at rank 2 when observer and target are grounded.
Living Statue is a real owned object form with safe return/expiry cleanup.
Related: HELP KITSTATUS.
~

0 KUEI-JIN KUEIJIN KUEIJINKIT~
Use KUEIJIN for the live kit menu, track training and dharma progression.
The kit has independent Chi/Dharma progression and 18 tracks, including
Blood/Bone/Jade/Flesh/Ghost Shintai, Yin/Yang/Hun/Po, noble disciplines,
battle aspects, spirit senses, travel, healing, chi crafting and Akuma.
These are Genesis effects, not reused Vampire progression or flags.
Use the live menu for the full ability list and current focus/costs.
